-- title:
--   Freeness of diamond automorphisms at the cusp, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta=\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ equal to `laurentBaseChange L` of `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over which $L$ is its fraction field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$. Let $j\in K$, assumed non-zero, have Laurent series the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion `jq` of the $j$-invariant. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ such that (i) $\sigma x=x$ for every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series lies in `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull (q^2*M'))`, the subfield generated over $L$ by the images of the expansions $j(\mathsf q^d)$ for $d\mid q^2M'$; and (ii) for every $b$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $j^{-1}$ (the chart algebra `chartAlgInf A K j`), the $0$-th Laurent coefficient of $\sigma b$ lies in $\operatorname{algebraMap} A\,L(\mathfrak m_A)$ if and only if that of $b$ does. Then $\sigma$ is the identity automorphism.
--
--   This is the $q=2$ case of the assertion that the diamond group of the covering $X_H(q^2M')\to X_0(q^2M')$ acts freely at the reduction of the cusp $\infty$: an $L$-automorphism of the level-$\Gamma_H$ function field that fixes the full modular function field of level $q^2M'$ and preserves the cusp prime $\mathfrak n=\{b:\ b(0)\in\mathfrak m_A\}$ of the pole chart is trivial. It feeds the construction of an element of the pole chart whose zeroth coefficient avoids $\mathfrak m_A$ along the minimal primes above the ideal generated by the inverse of the $j$-invariant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_eq_refl_of_forall_apply_eq_of_forall_coeff_zero_mem_iff_chartAlgInf_xH_of_eq_two.lean

